    "updated_at": "2023-01-14T06:52:59Z",
    "body": "Thanks, I'll file feedback as well as for #543 in time for Unicode's April meeting.\r\n\r\nIn my experience of trying to make IDNA interoperable over the past decade browsers have not been super opinionated on ToASCII. (Now ToUnicode is another matter, but that algorithm isn't directly exposed.) As long as we err on the side of compatibility, i.e., making hosts resolve, I think it should work out.\r\n\r\nAnd apparently the IETF hasn't been opinionated enough either as according to a comment in that other issue they gave up on standardizing the details of client behavior with IDNA2008. So I'm very thankful we have UTS46.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
